# Supply-chain posture (CISO pass 2026-11-04, docs/audits/2026-11-04-ciso-security-audit.md §2/§6).
#
# ignore-scripts: the Shai-Hulud waves (Sep 2025 → Aug 2026) propagate through
# `preinstall`/`postinstall`. Nothing this tree depends on needs an install script
# (measured 2026-11-04 with `npm query ':attr(scripts,[postinstall])'` — the only hit,
# unrs-resolver, is a no-op fallback because its platform binding ships as an
# optionalDependency). CI (`npm ci`), Vercel's install and local installs all read
# this file, so a dependency that later ADDS an install script does nothing until
# someone deliberately allows it here. `npm run <script>` / `npm test` still run.
ignore-scripts=true

# min-release-age: do not resolve a version published less than 7 days ago (npm ≥ 11.10;
# older npm warns "Unknown project config" and ignores it). A committed lockfile means
# `npm ci` is unaffected; this bounds `npm install`/`npm update`, which is where a
# freshly-poisoned release would enter. (Dependabot has its own `cooldown` setting.)
min-release-age=7
